BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:After the Bell: A K-12 & Dartmouth Connection Social
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261119T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261119T180000
DTSTAMP:20261114T165346Z
UID:guarini-53148@free-food-dartmouth
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://guarinigrad.dartmouth.edu/eve
 nts/2026/11/19/after-the-bell-a-k-12-dartmouth-connection-social/\nhttps:/
 /docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdLOZe9qHAERILPvWkp25NA1CkpIpuDa5H5fVMvE
 Ok9D_-Ppg/viewform\nhttps://forms.gle/Q3V1rM3GauZiH4Eo7\nhttps://home.dart
 mouth.edu/news/2026/08/dartmouth-launches-k-12-community-partnership\nhttp
 s://guarinigrad.dartmouth.edu\n\nDescription:\nAfter the Bell: A K-12 & Da
 rtmouth Connection Social\nis a meet-and-greet that brings together Dartmo
 uth faculty\, staff\, and students with educators from across the Upper Va
 lley. It will provide a great chance to talk with teachers who are excited
  to bring new ideas into their classrooms\, explore potential partnerships
 \, share your research or areas of expertise\, and learn about the needs a
 nd interests of local schools. Whether you’re already involved in K-12 o
 utreach or just curious about getting started\, we’d love to see you the
 re.\nEvent Details\nThursday\, November 19\, 2026 | 4-6 p.m.\nAtrium of th
 e Engineering & Computer Science Center (ECSC)\, on the west end of campus
 \nSnacks and beverages provided\nRSVP by Friday\, October 23\, 2026 using 
 this link:\nhttps://forms.gle/Q3V1rM3GauZiH4Eo7\nJoin the Dartmouth Partne
 rs Directory\n*\nSince the\nlaunch of the K-12 Community-Dartmouth Partner
 ship\nin August\, our school partners have shared that they’d like more 
 ways to connect with us. Two ideas they raised were programming such as th
 is event and a\nDartmouth Partners Directory\n\, a resource to help them f
 ind colleagues interested in working with schools.\nIf you’d like to be 
 included\, the RSVP form has a short section asking:\nBroadly speaking\, w
 hat area do you work in?\nWhat is your specific field or area?\nBrief desc
 ription of your work and how you’d like to engage with K-12 educators\n.
  A sentence or two is fine.\nGrade level(s) you’d like to engage with?\n
 Others you’d like to connect with beyond classroom teachers?\n*Note that
  you don’t need to attend the event to be listed in the directory.\nPlea
 se feel free to share this invitation with colleagues who might be interes
 ted\, and reach out with any questions!\n\nSource: Guarini\n\nWhy this was
  included: food keyword near service context\n\nFood availability is infer
 red from the source listing\; verify details before attending.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261114T165346Z
LOCATION:Atrium of the Engineering & Computer Science Center (ECSC)
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://guarinigrad.dartmouth.edu/events/2026/11/19/after-the-bell-a-k
 -12-dartmouth-connection-social/
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
END:VEVENT
